{"repositoryId":371836126,"availability":"available","full":"brandonjcampbell/Silky","name":"Silky","description":"A narrative development assistant: a word processor for fiction whose document is a graph. Write on a blank page; the story bible builds itself behind you. Runs in the browser.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2021-05-28T23:04:20Z","updated":"2026-10-18T07:46:03Z","license":"CC0-1.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://brandonjcampbell.github.io/Silky/","topics":["cytoscape","fiction","indexeddb","knowledge-graph","llm","neo4j","novel-writing","pwa","react","story-bible","storytelling","webgpu","writing-tools"],"demo":"https://brandonjcampbell.github.io/Silky/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T22:44:57.965Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T22:44:57.965Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T22:44:57.965Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T22:44:57.965Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A narrative development assistant. Write prose on a blank page; the story bible — people, places, facts, scenes, threads — builds itself behind you, and you can read it back as a manuscript, a wiki, a graph, a map or a timeline. Runs in your browser, nothing to install.","Most writing tools are a stack of pages, and most \"AI writing tools\" put a model in front of the writer. Silky does neither. It is a word processor for fiction whose document is a graph: the things in your story are nodes, the prose hangs off them, and an assistant called Spinner keeps the graph honest as you type — noticing who has walked into a scene, what has just become true, which chapter a scene belongs to — without ever writing your book for you unless you ask. Everything stays in your browser (or a folder you choose); nothing is uploaded anywhere."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brandonjcampbell/Silky/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"73fa508cfd